      "facts": [
        "What a skill may be called. Narrow on purpose: a name holds no user prose, so a refusal may quote it back (see `invalidSkillsRefusal`) and a file written under it cannot escape its directory.",
        "The 400 for a skills payload the schema refuses, naming where it was refused.",
        "The one issue worth reporting out of a list: the deepest path, since that is the field the payload got furthest into, with a union replaced by the issue of the branch it came closest to matching.",
        "The branch that complained least, which is the one the payload was closest to being. Without this an encoding fault in the base64 upload would be reported as the missing `revision` of the plain upload it is not.",
        "The payload's own name for a skill, only when it is still a legal one."
      ],
